{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "def is_Monotonic(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given array is monotonic (non-increasing or non-decreasing).\n    An empty array or a single-element array is considered monotonic.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(array) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    is_non_decreasing = True\n    is_non_increasing = True\n\n    for i in range(1, len(array)):\n        if array[i] < array[i-1]:\n            is_non_decreasing = False\n        if array[i] > array[i-1]:\n            is_non_increasing = False\n\n    return is_non_decreasing or is_non_increasing"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/71", "solution": "def comb_sort(list_of_elements):\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of comparable elements in ascending order using the Comb Sort algorithm.\n    The original input list remains unchanged.\"\"\"\n    n = len(list_of_elements)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    data = list_of_elements[:]  # Create a shallow copy to preserve the original list\n    \n    gap = n\n    shrink_factor = 1.3\n    swapped = True\n\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        gap = int(gap / shrink_factor)\n        if gap < 1:\n            gap = 1\n\n        swapped = False\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if data[i] > data[i + gap]:\n                data[i], data[i + gap] = data[i + gap], data[i]\n                swapped = True\n    \n    return data"}
