{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "from typing import List\n\n# The Newman-Conway sequence is defined as:\n# P(1) = 1\n# P(2) = 1\n# P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n - P(n-1)) for n > 2\n\nclass NewmanConwaySequence:\n    \"\"\"Computes and memoizes terms of the Newman-Conway sequence.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        # self._sequence[k-1] stores the value of P(k).\n        # Initialize with P(1) and P(2).\n        self._sequence: List[int] = [1, 1]\n\n    def _calculate_term(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the nth term of the Newman-Conway sequence, assuming n is positive.\"\"\"\n        # If the term is already computed, return it from the memoization list.\n        if n <= len(self._sequence):\n            return self._sequence[n - 1]\n\n        # Compute terms iteratively up to n.\n        # We start from the next term to compute (index len(self._sequence) + 1).\n        for i in range(len(self._sequence) + 1, n + 1):\n            # To compute P(i), we need P(i-1) which is already in self._sequence at index (i-1)-1.\n            p_i_minus_1_val = self._sequence[i - 2]\n\n            # First term in the formula: P(P(i-1))\n            term1 = self._sequence[p_i_minus_1_val - 1]\n\n            # Second term in the formula: P(i - P(i-1))\n            term2 = self._sequence[(i - p_i_minus_1_val) - 1]\n            \n            current_term = term1 + term2\n            self._sequence.append(current_term)\n        \n        # After the loop, the nth term is at self._sequence[n-1].\n        return self._sequence[n - 1]\n\n# Create a module-level instance of the calculator for memoization across calls.\n_newman_conway_calculator_instance = NewmanConwaySequence()\n\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence.\n    The sequence is 1-indexed, with P(1)=1 and P(2)=1.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _newman_conway_calculator_instance._calculate_term(n)"}
