{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is undulating, meaning its digits strictly alternate between increasing and decreasing.\n    An undulating number must have at least two digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_num = str(number)\n    n = len(s_num)\n\n    # BR3: A number must contain at least two digits.\n    if n < 2:\n        return False\n\n    # Convert digits to integers for easier comparison.\n    digits = [int(digit_char) for digit_char in s_num]\n\n    # For a two-digit number, it's undulating if the digits are different (BR2).\n    if n == 2:\n        return digits[0] != digits[1]\n\n    # Initialize the trend based on the first two digits.\n    # If the first two digits are equal, they cannot establish an alternating pattern (violates BR2 implicitly).\n    if digits[0] == digits[1]:\n        return False\n\n    # 'is_increasing_segment' tracks the trend from digits[i-1] to digits[i].\n    # True if digits[i-1] < digits[i], False if digits[i-1] > digits[i].\n    is_increasing_segment = (digits[1] > digits[0])\n\n    # Iterate from the third digit (index 2) to the last.\n    for i in range(2, n):\n        current_digit = digits[i]\n        prev_digit = digits[i-1]\n\n        # If any adjacent digits are equal, the strict alternation is broken.\n        # This covers BR2 for all digits against their immediate neighbors.\n        if current_digit == prev_digit:\n            return False\n\n        # If the previous segment was increasing (e.g., d[i-2] < d[i-1]),\n        # the current segment must be decreasing (d[i-1] > d[i]) to form a peak.\n        if is_increasing_segment:\n            if current_digit > prev_digit:\n                return False  # The trend continued increasing, not alternating.\n            # Trend successfully switched to decreasing.\n            is_increasing_segment = False\n        # If the previous segment was decreasing (e.g., d[i-2] > d[i-1]),\n        # the current segment must be increasing (d[i-1] < d[i]) to form a valley.\n        else: # is_decreasing_segment\n            if current_digit < prev_digit:\n                return False  # The trend continued decreasing, not alternating.\n            # Trend successfully switched to increasing.\n            is_increasing_segment = True\n\n    # If the loop completes without returning False, the number is undulating.\n    return True"}
