{"task_id": "Mbpp/94", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Optional\n\ndef index_minimum(tuples: List[Tuple[str, int]]) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the first value of the tuple with the smallest second value.\n    Handles empty lists by returning None, and ties by returning the first encountered.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not tuples:\n        return None\n\n    min_second_value = math.inf\n    result_first_value = None\n\n    for first, second in tuples:\n        if second < min_second_value:\n            min_second_value = second\n            result_first_value = first\n            \n    return result_first_value"}
