{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m) using dynamic programming.\n    a(n, m) is the number of permutations of {1, ..., n} with m ascents.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a 2D DP table to store Eulerian numbers a(i, j)\n    # The table size is (n+1) x (n+1) as m can go up to n-1.\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: a(0, 0) = 1\n    # This represents the single permutation of an empty set with 0 ascents.\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table using the recurrence relation\n    # a(i, j) = (j + 1) * a(i-1, j) + (i - j) * a(i-1, j-1)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(i):  # m must be less than n, so j ranges from 0 to i-1\n            # Term 1: (j + 1) * a(i-1, j)\n            term1 = (j + 1) * dp[i - 1][j]\n\n            # Term 2: (i - j) * a(i-1, j-1)\n            # This term is 0 if j-1 is out of bounds (i.e., j=0)\n            term2 = 0\n            if j - 1 >= 0:\n                term2 = (i - j) * dp[i - 1][j - 1]\n            \n            dp[i][j] = term1 + term2\n            \n    return dp[n][m]"}
