{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "def find_length(binaryString: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum difference between the number of 0s and 1s in any substring.\n    This uses a variant of Kadane's algorithm, mapping '0' to 1 and '1' to -1 to find the maximum sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_so_far = 0\n    current_max = 0\n\n    for char in binaryString:\n        if char == '0':\n            current_max += 1\n        else:  # char == '1'\n            current_max -= 1\n        \n        if current_max < 0:\n            current_max = 0\n        \n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n            \n    return max_so_far"}
