{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(array: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Find the first occurrence of the element using binary search\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    first_occurrence = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            first_occurrence = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    if first_occurrence == -1:  # Element not found\n        return False\n\n    # Find the last occurrence of the element using binary search\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    last_occurrence = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            last_occurrence = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    count = last_occurrence - first_occurrence + 1\n    return count > n // 2"}
