{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    Uses dynamic programming to compute lengths for all substrings.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of substring s[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromes of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the table for substrings of length 2 to n\n    # 'length' is the length of the substring (j - i + 1)\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If characters match, they form part of the palindrome.\n                # Add 2 to the LPS of the inner substring s[i+1...j-1].\n                # If i+1 > j-1 (i.e., length is 2 and no inner substring), dp[i+1][j-1] will be 0.\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                # If characters don't match, we must exclude either s[i] or s[j].\n                # Take the maximum of LPS of s[i+1...j] and s[i...j-1].\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    # The result is the LPS of the entire string s[0...n-1]\n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
