{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef max_sum(array: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence in the given array.\n    A bitonic subsequence is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return array[0]\n\n    inc = [0] * n\n    dec = [0] * n\n\n    # Compute maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at each index i\n    for i in range(n):\n        inc[i] = array[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if array[j] < array[i]:\n                inc[i] = max(inc[i], inc[j] + array[i])\n\n    # Compute maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at each index i\n    for i in reversed(range(n)):\n        dec[i] = array[i]\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if array[j] < array[i]:\n                dec[i] = max(dec[i], dec[j] + array[i])\n\n    # Combine increasing and decreasing sums to find the maximum bitonic sum\n    max_bitonic = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Subtract array[i] because it's included in both inc[i] and dec[i] as the peak\n        max_bitonic = max(max_bitonic, inc[i] + dec[i] - array[i])\n\n    return max_bitonic"}
