{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple, Optional\n\ndef max_aggregate(input_list: List[Tuple[str, int]]) -> Optional[Tuple[str, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the name with the maximum aggregate score from a list of (name, score) tuples.\n    Scores for the same name are summed. Returns None if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return None\n\n    aggregates = {}\n    for name, score in input_list:\n        aggregates[name] = aggregates.get(name, 0) + score\n\n    max_name, max_score = max(aggregates.items(), key=lambda item: item[1])\n    return (max_name, max_score)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/301", "solution": "def dict_depth(data: dict) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum depth of nested dictionaries.\n    An empty dictionary has a depth of 0; a dictionary with no nested dictionaries has a depth of 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not data:\n        return 0\n\n    max_child_depth = 0\n    for value in data.values():\n        if isinstance(value, dict):\n            child_depth = dict_depth(value)\n            max_child_depth = max(max_child_depth, child_depth)\n\n    return 1 + max_child_depth"}
