{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(values: list[int], length: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence that includes values[k],\n    where prefix elements are from indices 0 to i and suffix elements are from indices k+1 to length-1.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # dp_prefix[j] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at j,\n    # using elements from 0 to i, such that all elements are strictly less than values[k].\n    prefix_dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n    max_prefix_sum_val = 0\n\n    # Calculate max sum for increasing subsequence from prefix 0...i\n    # The subsequence must consist of elements strictly less than values[k].\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if values[j] < values[k]:\n            current_sum_ending_at_j = values[j]\n            for p in range(j):\n                if values[p] < values[j]:\n                    current_sum_ending_at_j = max(current_sum_ending_at_j, prefix_dp[p] + values[j])\n            prefix_dp[j] = current_sum_ending_at_j\n            max_prefix_sum_val = max(max_prefix_sum_val, prefix_dp[j])\n        else:\n            # This element cannot be part of the IS that comes before values[k]\n            prefix_dp[j] = 0 \n\n    # suffix_dp[j] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence starting at j,\n    # using elements from k+1 to length-1, such that all elements are strictly greater than values[k].\n    suffix_dp = [0] * length\n    max_suffix_sum_val = 0\n\n    # Calculate max sum for increasing subsequence from suffix k+1...length-1\n    # The subsequence must consist of elements strictly greater than values[k].\n    # Iterate in reverse to build the \"increasing\" subsequence starting at j.\n    for j in range(length - 1, k, -1): \n        if values[j] > values[k]:\n            current_sum_starting_at_j = values[j]\n            for p in range(length - 1, j, -1):\n                if values[p] > values[j]:\n                    current_sum_starting_at_j = max(current_sum_starting_at_j, suffix_dp[p] + values[j])\n            suffix_dp[j] = current_sum_starting_at_j\n            max_suffix_sum_val = max(max_suffix_sum_val, suffix_dp[j])\n        else:\n            # This element cannot be part of the IS that comes after values[k]\n            suffix_dp[j] = 0 \n\n    # The total maximum sum combines the best prefix sum, values[k], and the best suffix sum.\n    return max_prefix_sum_val + values[k] + max_suffix_sum_val"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/309", "solution": "from dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass\nclass Number:\n    value: float\n\nclass MaxCalculator:\n    def compute(self, a: Number, b: Number) -> Number:\n        if a.value > b.value:\n            return a\n        else:\n            return b\n\ndef maximum(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum of two numbers using Number and MaxCalculator classes.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_a = Number(a)\n    num_b = Number(b)\n    calculator = MaxCalculator()\n    result_number = calculator.compute(num_a, num_b)\n    return result_number.value"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "import heapq\n\ndef large_product(list_a: list[int], list_b: list[int], k: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the specified number of largest products from two given lists, selecting one factor from each list.\n    Uses a min-heap to efficiently keep track of the top k products.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_a or not list_b or k == 0:\n        return []\n\n    min_heap = []\n    \n    for a in list_a:\n        for b in list_b:\n            product = a * b\n            if len(min_heap) < k:\n                heapq.heappush(min_heap, product)\n            elif product > min_heap[0]:\n                heapq.heapreplace(min_heap, product)\n    \n    # The heap contains the k largest products, but in arbitrary order (smallest of k at root).\n    # Pop them and reverse to get descending order.\n    result = []\n    while min_heap:\n        result.append(heapq.heappop(min_heap))\n    \n    return result[::-1]"}
