{"task_id": "Mbpp/426", "solution": "class Number:\n    def __init__(self, value):\n        self.value = value\n\n    def is_odd(self):\n        return self.value % 2 != 0\n\nclass NumberList:\n    def __init__(self, numbers_raw):\n        \"\"\"Converts a list of raw integers into a list of Number objects.\"\"\"\n        self.numbers = [Number(n) for n in numbers_raw]\n\n    def get_numbers(self):\n        return self.numbers\n\nclass OddNumberFilter:\n    def filter(self, input_list_raw):\n        \"\"\"Filters the given list, returning only the odd numbers.\"\"\"\n        number_list_obj = NumberList(input_list_raw)\n        odd_numbers = []\n        for number_obj in number_list_obj.get_numbers():\n            if number_obj.is_odd():\n                odd_numbers.append(number_obj.value)\n        return odd_numbers\n\ndef filter_oddnumbers(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters a list of numbers, returning only the odd numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_filter = OddNumberFilter()\n    return odd_filter.filter(input_list)"}
