{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(lst: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list using the Shell sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new sorted list, preserving the original.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(lst)\n    # Create a shallow copy to ensure the original list is not modified.\n    arr = lst[:]\n\n    # Start with a large gap and then reduce it.\n    gap = n // 2\n    while gap > 0:\n        # Perform a gapped insertion sort for the current gap size.\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = arr[i]\n            j = i\n            # Shift elements that are greater than temp to the right.\n            while j >= gap and arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                arr[j] = arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            arr[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2\n    return arr"}
