{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "import re\nimport string\n\ndef find_adverb_position(sentence: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first adverb and its positions in a given sentence.\n    An adverb is identified by a simple heuristic: a word (after stripping punctuation)\n    that is longer than two characters and ends with 'ly' (case-insensitive).\n    \"\"\"\n    for match in re.finditer(r'\\S+', sentence):\n        raw_word = match.group(0)\n        word_start_index = match.start()\n\n        cleaned_word = raw_word.strip(string.punctuation)\n\n        if len(cleaned_word) > 2 and cleaned_word.lower().endswith('ly'):\n            adverb_text = cleaned_word\n            adverb_end_index = word_start_index + len(adverb_text)\n            return (word_start_index, adverb_end_index, adverb_text)\n\n    return ()"}
