{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P0 to Pn inclusive.\n    Raises ValueError if n is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 3 # P0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 3 # P0 + P1 = 3 + 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 5 # P0 + P1 + P2 = 3 + 0 + 2\n\n    # Initialize current sum with P0 + P1 + P2\n    total_sum = 5\n\n    # Initialize the last three Perrin numbers to calculate subsequent ones\n    p_minus_3 = 3  # Represents P(i-3), initially P0\n    p_minus_2 = 0  # Represents P(i-2), initially P1\n    p_minus_1 = 2  # Represents P(i-1), initially P2\n\n    # Calculate and sum Perrin numbers from P3 up to Pn\n    for _ in range(3, n + 1):\n        p_current = p_minus_3 + p_minus_2\n        total_sum += p_current\n        # Shift values for the next iteration\n        p_minus_3 = p_minus_2\n        p_minus_2 = p_minus_1\n        p_minus_1 = p_current\n\n    return total_sum"}
