{"task_id": "Mbpp/453", "solution": "import math\n\ndef sumofFactors(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all even factors of a given positive integer.\n    The algorithm iterates up to the square root of n to find factor pairs.\n    \"\"\"\n    total = 0\n    # Iterate from 2 up to the integer square root of n to find factors and their complements.\n    for i in range(2, math.isqrt(n) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            # If i is an even factor, add it to the total.\n            if i % 2 == 0:\n                total += i\n            \n            # Compute the complementary factor j = n // i.\n            # If j is even and different from i (to avoid double counting for perfect squares), add it.\n            j = n // i\n            if j % 2 == 0 and j != i:\n                total += j\n    \n    # The number n itself is always a factor. If n is even, add it.\n    # This covers cases where n is prime and even (e.g., n=2), or when n is the complement of 1 (an odd factor).\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        total += n\n        \n    return total"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/454", "solution": "import re\n\nWORD_SPLIT_REGEX = re.compile(r\"\\b\\w+\\b\", re.UNICODE)\n\ndef text_match_wordz(input_str: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns True if the input string contains a word with 'z', False otherwise.\n    Words are delimited by whitespace or punctuation; the check is case-sensitive.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_str:\n        return False\n\n    words = WORD_SPLIT_REGEX.findall(input_str)\n\n    for word in words:\n        if 'z' in word:\n            return True\n    return False"}
