{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "def combinations_list(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds all possible combinations of elements from a given list,\n    ordered by length and then by the original order of elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    combinations = [[]]\n    for item in input_list:\n        # For each existing combination, create a new one by prepending the current item.\n        new_combinations_with_item = []\n        for existing_combo in combinations:\n            new_combinations_with_item.append([item] + existing_combo)\n        # Extend the main list of combinations with these newly formed ones.\n        combinations.extend(new_combinations_with_item)\n    return combinations"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "import math\n\ndef max_subarray_product(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum product of any contiguous subarray within the given array.\n    This implementation uses O(n) time and O(1) space.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nums:\n        return 0\n\n    max_prod = nums[0]\n    min_prod = nums[0]\n    result = nums[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(nums)):\n        val = nums[i]\n        \n        # If current number is negative, swap max_prod and min_prod\n        # because a negative number can turn a small negative into a large positive\n        if val < 0:\n            max_prod, min_prod = min_prod, max_prod\n        \n        # update max_prod and min_prod for the current number\n        max_prod = max(val, max_prod * val)\n        min_prod = min(val, min_prod * val)\n        \n        # update the overall maximum product\n        result = max(result, max_prod)\n        \n    return result"}
