{"task_id": "Mbpp/564", "solution": "def count_Pairs(input_list: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of unordered pairs of distinct elements in a list of integers.\n    The time complexity is O(n^2).\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    n = len(input_list)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if input_list[i] != input_list[j]:\n                count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/566", "solution": "class Number:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates an integer value.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: int):\n        if not isinstance(value, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"Number value must be an integer\")\n        if value < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Number must be non-negative\")\n        self.value = value\n\nclass DigitSumCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Provides logic to compute the sum of decimal digits.\"\"\"\n    @staticmethod\n    def sumDigits(number: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Return the sum of the decimal digits of a non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n        return sum(int(d) for d in str(number))\n\ndef sum_digits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Public API to compute the sum of digits of a non-negative integer.\n    Orchestrates validation and computation, returning the result.\n    \"\"\"\n    num = Number(number)\n    return DigitSumCalculator.sumDigits(num.value)"}
