{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "import math\n\ndef wind_chill(wind_velocity_kmh: float, temperature_celsius: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the wind chill index rounded to the next integer.\n    Uses the specified formula with wind velocity in km/h and temperature in Celsius.\n    \"\"\"\n    # WCI = 13.12 + 0.6215*T - 11.37*V^0.16 + 0.3965*T*V^0.16\n    # where T is temperature in Celsius and V is wind speed in km/h.\n    \n    # The formula is typically for wind speed in m/s, but the design context states V is in km/h.\n    # We will use the formula as given for V in km/h.\n    \n    # According to Environment Canada's official formula, the V (wind speed) should be in km/h\n    # for this specific formula.\n    \n    wci = 13.12 + (0.6215 * temperature_celsius) - (11.37 * (wind_velocity_kmh**0.16)) + \\\n          (0.3965 * temperature_celsius * (wind_velocity_kmh**0.16))\n    \n    return math.ceil(wci)"}
