{"task_id": "Mbpp/728", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef sum_list(a: List[int], b: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the element-wise sum of two lists of integers.\n    Raises ValueError if the input lists are not of equal length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(a) != len(b):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input lists must be of equal length.\")\n    return [x + y for x, y in zip(a, b)]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/730", "solution": "def consecutive_duplicates(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes consecutive duplicate elements from a given list, preserving order.\n    Returns a new list without modifying the original.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    result = [input_list[0]]\n    for i in range(1, len(input_list)):\n        if input_list[i] != result[-1]:\n            result.append(input_list[i])\n    return result"}
