{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(lst, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by k positions, returning a new list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return []\n\n    n = len(lst)\n    k_effective = k % n\n\n    if k_effective == 0:\n        return list(lst)  # Return a shallow copy if no effective rotation\n\n    # The elements from the end up to k_effective positions\n    # go to the front, followed by the remaining elements.\n    return lst[-k_effective:] + lst[:-k_effective]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/748", "solution": "def capital_words_spaces(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Inserts spaces before capital letters in a string, except for the first character.\n    Handles empty strings and strings with no capital letters after the first.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return \"\"\n\n    result_chars = []\n    for i, char in enumerate(input_string):\n        if i > 0 and char.isupper():\n            result_chars.append(' ')\n        result_chars.append(char)\n    \n    return \"\".join(result_chars)"}
