{"task_id": "Mbpp/788", "solution": "def new_tuple(input_list, input_string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Creates a new tuple by appending a string to elements of a list.\n    The order of elements from the list is preserved, followed by the string.\n    \"\"\"\n    return tuple(input_list + [input_string])"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "def right_insertion(sorted_list, value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the index at which `value` should be inserted into `sorted_list`\n    to maintain ascending order. The function does not modify the list.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, len(sorted_list)\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if sorted_list[mid] <= value:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low"}
