{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(array: list[int], element: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Assumes the input array is sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n    if n == 0:\n        return -1\n\n    # Check if the array is sorted (as per FR5 and System Implementation)\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        if array[i] > array[i+1]:\n            raise ValueError(\"Array must be sorted in ascending order.\")\n\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Try to find further occurrences on the right\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result"}
